                <pb facs="0536" n="440" sameAs="frus:frus1899/pg440"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Governor
                            Foster, of Louisiana.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1899-07-22"><hi rendition="#italic">July 22,
                        1899</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Italian chargé requests report on alleged lynching at Tallulah of five Italians
                    and asks protection of any Italian subjects who may be <pb facs="0537" n="441"
                        xml:id="pg441"/> in danger. Were persons lynched Italian subjects or
                    naturalized Americans?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
